{"id": "b93b6150-a5c5-4631-b06f-b332540947b9", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "This is a broad, multi-dimensional review across six domains — I'll pull this together rather than doing it piecemeal. Let me survey your Firehose delivery streams and configuration first, then dig into health/performance metrics and quotas.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_5tadT2ZbMStHdVUobKPlfP", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Inventory all Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams in us-east-1 for account 462422900361 and assess security and reliability configuration posture.",
  "context": "User wants an operational review covering security, reliability, delivery health, performance, cost, and service quotas for all Firehose delivery streams in us-east-1. This is the inventory + security/reliability configuration slice of that review.",
  "resources": ["us-east-1", "462422900361", "Amazon Data Firehose / firehose service"],
  "timeframe": "current configuration state (not time-series)",
  "criteria": "For each delivery stream: list destination type (S3, Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, HTTP endpoint, etc.), encryption at rest (SSE) status and KMS key type, source (direct PUT vs Kinesis Data Stream), IAM role used and whether it's overly permissive, VPC delivery config if applicable, backup/error output S3 bucket config, buffering hints, compression, data transformation Lambda config, dynamic partitioning, retry duration settings, CloudWatch logging enabled/disabled, and tags. Flag anything indicating weak security posture (no encryption, missing backup, no error logging, wildcard IAM permissions) or reliability risk (short retry duration, no failover config, missing error output prefix)."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}, {"id": "tooluse_PEdr7vV99nsFTIOVzYtcx0", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Analyze CloudWatch metrics for delivery health, performance, and cost signals across all Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams in us-east-1, and check relevant service quotas/limits.",
  "context": "User wants an operational review covering delivery health, performance, cost, and service quotas for all Firehose delivery streams in us-east-1, account 462422900361. This is the metrics + quotas slice of that review; a separate pass is covering security/reliability configuration.",
  "resources": ["us-east-1", "462422900361", "Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams (namespace AWS/Firehose)"],
  "timeframe": "last 14 days, compare to prior 14 days as baseline where useful",
  "criteria": "For each delivery stream pull: DeliveryToS3.Success / DeliveryToDestination.Success rate, records/bytes throughput (IncomingRecords, IncomingBytes), DeliveryToS3.DataFreshness or destination-specific freshness metric, ThrottledRecords / ThrottledDescribeStream, error metrics like DeliveryToS3.DataFreshness spikes, retry counts, and any 4xx/5xx from destinations. For cost, note data volume trends and whether format conversion, compression, or dynamic partitioning is enabled (affects cost). For quotas, check current delivery stream count and throughput per stream against AWS Firehose service quotas (e.g., streams per account/region, PUT record throughput per stream) via service-quotas or documented defaults, and flag any stream close to a limit. Rate severity of each finding (critical/high/medium/low) based on impact to data delivery reliability or cost efficiency."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}], "created_at": null}
